        "content": "\n**Baseline: there are zero tests in this repository** — no `*.test.ts`/`*.spec.ts`, no `test_*.py`, no `__tests__/`, no test runner in `web/package.json` (no vitest/jest), no `pytest.ini`/`conftest.py`, no CI workflow. `pytest` is listed as an engine dev-dependency but unused.\n\nThe two layers are at very different stages, which changes what \"gap\" means for each:\n\n- **`web/`** — the server logic is *implemented* (sources, runs, rulesets, audit, auth, engine client, formatting, Zod contracts). This is real, shippable code with 0% coverage — the most urgent gap.\n- **`engine/`** — almost everything is a `NotImplementedError` stub (Phases 2/3/5/6 per `AGENTS.md`). Only `pipeline/schema.py` (Pydantic models + validators), `detect.py::severity_for_orphan`, `graph.py::should_auto_apply`, and the `main.py` route wiring are real. For the stubs, the useful \"test gap\" is writing the test *now*, from the spec in `AGENTS.md`, so implementation is TDD rather than untested-by-construction.\n\nI'll recommend a test runner for `web/` (none installed — **Vitest** would need your approval per the dependency policy before I add it) and note `httpx` is needed for `engine`'s FastAPI `TestClient` (also not currently a dependency).\n\n---\n\n",
