      {
        "title": "A2. DB-backed server functions — need a mocked/test Drizzle db",
        "content": "\nThese are untested and the highest-value gap in the whole repo, because they encode the table-ownership and reproducibility invariants `AGENTS.md` calls out as load-bearing.\n\n**`lib/server/rulesets.ts::createRulesetVersion`** — the most important one. Untested behaviors: version increments per-name (not globally), the previous active ruleset is deactivated, exactly one ruleset stays active system-wide, and the advisory lock actually serializes concurrent saves of the same name.\n\n```ts\n// web/lib/server/rulesets.test.ts (against a test Postgres schema, or a Drizzle mock)\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"starts a new name at version 1\", async () => { /* insert, assert version === 1 */ });\n  it(\"increments version per name, independent of other rulesets' versions\", async () => {\n    // create \"policy-a\" v1, v2; create \"policy-b\" v1 — assert policy-b.version === 1, not 3\n  });\n  it(\"deactivates the previously active ruleset when a new one is saved\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"never leaves two rulesets active at once\", async () => {\n    // create two different-named rulesets sequentially, assert only the latest isActive\n  });\n  it(\"two concurrent saves of the same name do not both get version N — INTEGRATION, needs a real DB\", async () => {\n    // Promise.all([createRulesetVersion(a), createRulesetVersion(a)]) -> versions must be {N, N+1}, not {N, N}\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/runs.ts`**:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"failUndispatchedRun\", () => {\n  it(\"marks a queued run as failed with the error and finishedAt set\", async () => {});\n  it(\"is a no-op once the engine has advanced the run past queued — must not overwrite real progress\", async () => {\n    // seed a run with status \"matching\"; call failUndispatchedRun; assert status is UNCHANGED\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getSeverityBreakdown\", () => {\n  it(\"returns all-zero breakdown for a run with no conflicts\", async () => {});\n  it(\"drops a conflict row with a severity outside 1..4 rather than widening the histogram (engine-bug case)\", async () => {\n    // insert a conflicts row with severity=9 via raw SQL (bypassing the app's own validation);\n    // getSeverityBreakdown must not include it and must not throw\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createRun\", () => {\n  it(\"always starts at status=queued with EMPTY_RUN_STATS regardless of input\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/sources.ts`**:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"findSourceIds\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty set for an empty input array without querying the db\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns only the ids that actually exist, silently dropping the rest\", async () => {\n    // findSourceIds([\"real-id\", \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"]) -> Set{\"real-id\"}\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets hubspot and salesforce as crm, databricks/snowflake as warehouse, synthetic separately\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/audit.ts`**:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"appendAudit\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults detail to {} and resolutionId to null when omitted\", async () => {});\n});\ndescribe(\"listRunAudit\", () => {\n  it(\"returns entries oldest-first (timeline order), not newest-first\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "A3. External I/O — need `fetch` mocking",
        "content": "\n**`lib/server/engine.ts`** — this is the single highest-value *error-handling* gap in the codebase: every failure mode of the web↔engine boundary is implemented but none is tested.\n\n```ts\n// web/lib/server/engine.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { startRun, fetchEngineStatus, EngineUnreachableError } from \"./engine\";\n\nbeforeEach(() => { process.env.ENGINE_URL = \"http://engine.test\"; });\n\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when ENGINE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    delete process.env.ENGINE_URL;\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).rejects.toThrow(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when the network call itself fails\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"ECONNREFUSED\")));\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).rejects.toThrow(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws with the timeout-specific message when the request aborts on timeout\", async () => {\n    const err = Object.assign(new Error(\"timed out\"), { name: \"TimeoutError\" });\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(err));\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).rejects.toThrow(/no response within 8s/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError on a non-2xx response, including the response body\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"bad runId\", { status: 422 })));\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).rejects.toThrow(/422/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when the engine returns 200 with a body that violates the tool contract\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ ok: true }))); // wrong shape\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).rejects.toThrow(/tool contract/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"resolves cleanly on a well-formed 200\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ runId: \"id\", accepted: true })));\n    await expect(startRun(\"id\")).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not a throw) when the engine is unreachable — polling must degrade gracefully\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"down\")));\n    expect(await fetchEngineStatus(\"id\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null on a non-2xx status\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(null, { status: 500 })));\n    expect(await fetchEngineStatus(\"id\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when the 200 body fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ garbage: true })));\n    expect(await fetchEngineStatus(\"id\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/auth.ts`** — mock `@clerk/nextjs/server`:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws when there is no authenticated session (proxy.ts/handler disagreement case)\", async () => {\n    // mock auth() -> { isAuthenticated: false }\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n  it(\"resolves username/email/id via reviewerLabel precedence\", async () => { /* mock currentUser() variants */ });\n});\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not a throw) when signed out\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "A4. Route handlers — request/response contract",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// web/app/api/sources/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"POST /api/sources\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 400 with field issues for an invalid body, and never calls createSource\", async () => {});\n  it(\"returns 201 and the created row for a valid body\", async () => {});\n  it(\"rejects a body containing a credential-shaped field (password/token/secret) — defense in depth for the 'never store secrets' rule\", async () => {\n    // createSourceSchema has no such field, so this should already 400 — assert it, don't assume it\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "A5. Middleware",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// web/proxy.test.ts — exercise the matcher/isPublicRoute logic directly\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\"%s is public\", (p) => {});\n  it.each([\"/runs\", \"/api/sources\", \"/conflicts/123\"])(\"%s requires auth\", (p) => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Part B — Engine layer (`engine/`), mostly unimplemented",
        "content": "\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "B1. Already-implemented, untested today",
        "content": "\n```python\n",
        "level": 3
